class_name SkelAnim
## Bone-track animation factory for the skeletal characters. Clips are
## authored as per-bone euler DELTAS (degrees) composed onto the skeleton's
## rest pose at build time, so one table set serves every archetype (scaled
## by amp/sway) and pose iteration never leaves Godot.
##
## Bone-local frames at rest (all bones, Godot terms — derived from the
## armature in kit_skel.py, roll 0):
##   spine chain (hips/spine/chest/head): like Node3D — +X leans back,
##     -X bows forward, +Y turns left, +Z tilts left.
##   limbs (uarm/farm/hand/thigh/shin): Y runs along the bone (down at
##     rest); +X swings the limb tip FORWARD, -X backward. Elbows flex +X,
##     knees flex -X. ±Z sideways: outward is -Z on the right limb, +Z on
##     the left. foot: +X lifts the toes.
##   hips position deltas are in skeleton space: +Y up, +Z backward.
##
## Attacks use the shared 35% windup / ~15% hit / settle shape; combat code
## time-scales playback to the weapon's windup/active/recover numbers.

## clip -> { "len": s, "loop": bool, "bones": {bone: [[t, x, y, z]...]},
##           "pos": {bone: [[t, dx, dy, dz]...]} }
